WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.030
<i>We've been waiting and waiting 
for this summer vacation!</i>

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.360
<i>It's the beginning of Shonan's top season,</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.620
<i>and, of course, I'm going to be immersed 
in surfing all day every day.</i>

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.000
Wow! It's crowded again today!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.580
Come, o Azure Wolf!

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.870
Passionate Sapphire!

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.250
Naoya!

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.260
Your board really stands out, 
so I knew it was you right away, Naoya.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.060
And your tricks are as cool as ever!

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.640
So what brought you here all of a sudden?

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.640
Fanmeet.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.980
Fanmeet?

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.560
A fan meeting.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.140
A fanmeet for Miruru.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.620
Really?

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.150
So, that's why you made the trip 
to the big city all the way from Oita?

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.480
Yeah. Also, to watch this 
season's anime in real time.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.280
I really hate getting 
spoiled on social media.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.050
I see you love anime as much as ever.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.780
I have to get going soon.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.640
Later!

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.980
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:45.010
Wave 8   My Guardian Spirit

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.420
So, this is Oita's famous 
candied pomelo peel, is it?

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.780
It's good!

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.020
Yeah! It'd run a pretty close race 
with dried sweet potatoes!

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.460
You really bought a lot there.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.030
So cute!

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.620
The one that's on now is 
<i>Miruru Chronicle</i>, right?

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.420
Yeah.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.330
When Sakura was little, 
she really loved Miruru, too.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:16.090
I started watching recently 
because of Naoya. It's pretty fun.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.720
<i>Magical Maid Miruru</i> appeals 
to everyone from children to adults!

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.120
It's a super popular 
magical girl anime series!

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.690
Every year, the worldview 
and buddies may change,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.180
but having Miruru as the lead 
is consistent and never changes.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.450
Miruru is an eternal and immortal existence!

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:35.440
And it's an ambitious project that defies 
the conventional wisdom of the industry.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.270
I really do want you to watch it 
properly from the first season.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.740
The season I recommend 
the most is the second, but...

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.730
I-I see.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:45.750
Naoya-san, it seems that Miruru lies 
at the center of your world.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.200
At the center of my world is...

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:50.700
Right now, it's this!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.420
Forest Cup in Tsurigasaki!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.460
I'm going to win this no matter what!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.890
Really? Win? Well, do your best then.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:00.780
Naoya! You're my rival too, understand?

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.840
I haven't forgotten 
that I lost to you in Oarai!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.920
Next time, I will beat you!

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.860
There's no way we'll lose, is there, Miruru?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.960
After all, Miruru is my guardian spirit.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.900
Dreams and hope... Miruru is the one 
who taught me about all of that.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.470
So I have to beat 
the two of you together, huh?

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.360
You really are a tough opponent.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.550
We're going to start the viewing party soon.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.470
Starting with season one.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.370
Let's see...

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.870
<b>Magical Maid\h
 Miruru</b>

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.870
<b>Magical Maid\h
 Miruru</b>

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.380
Possibilities...

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.880
...are infinite!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.130
MiruMiru! MaiMai!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.500
Revolution Change!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.900
This is our final battle!

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.650
We will not be defeated 
by any twists of fate!

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.160
Together, we will overcome any pain!

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.080
Naoya-san?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.070
What's wrong?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.580
Two things I thought would always 
be there... waves and my fave...

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.710
Naoya?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.020
Miruru... might end this year.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:02.840
What?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:08.840
Last night, I was texting some people 
I met at the fanmeet, and it came up.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.900
And now that they mention it,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.700
the "chronicle" in the title does seem 
to have some hidden significance,

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.710
and there are episodes 
that seem to foreshadow it,

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.200
and it's the fifth year, 
so it's a good place to stop.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.950
I don't really understand, but...

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.030
There hasn't been 
an announcement yet, right?

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.290
Theories are just theories in the end.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.960
Until there's an official announcement, 
it's better not to think too much about it.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.260
For now, you should pour 
everything you've got into practice.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.950
All right!

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.250
Hup!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:39.620
Yeah!

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.420
Miruru!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.520
I'm heading in.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.850
I wonder if Naoya's okay...

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.380
How cute!

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.940
Just like Isokichi...

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:13.030
Huh? Isokichi?

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.500
Whoa...

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:21.900
How did you get here?

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.640
Big Brother!

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.800
Huh? Sakura?

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.300
Take that!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.350
He's amazing!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.060
Welcome, ladies!

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:43.320
Yay!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.900
Yay! Hug me! Hug me!

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.090
It's been a while.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:52.030
We haven't seen you since the party 
after the competition in Oarai, right?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.470
I'm happy to see you again.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.430
I'm so sorry for all the trouble 
my brother always causes you.

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:59.570
What? Why is that the first thing 
you're saying to them?

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.990
Honestly. If you're coming, 
you should tell me you're coming!

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:05.580
Tadao-san and I talked 
and decided to make it a surprise.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.680
Right?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.750
Yes!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.380
No surprise, no life!

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.590
You've gotten better 
at surfing, Big Brother!

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.100
Of course I have!

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.090
I'm aiming for the world, after all!

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.390
Oh, that's right!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.620
I was given a message to pass on to you.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.000
Huh?

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.150
Masaki-kun! You doing okay?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.360
Have you gotten used to Shonan?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.590
We're planning to go see 
the competition in Chiba.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.240
Make sure you practice hard, okay?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.370
You're Oarai's rising star! Aim for the top!

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:39.370
He said I'm a "rising star"!

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.730
Shoko-san! Manager!

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:45.670
I'm going to bring 
the winner's cup home to Oarai!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.720
There he goes, 
acting all cocky again. Right?

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.810
Just...

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.720
Is my big brother's board 
just like my big brother?

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:11.550
Yeah!

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.010
Even when he's way out in the ocean, 
you know it's him right away.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.540
Your personality tends to show through.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.970
Oh, right!

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:19.390
Naoya-san, your board is really cute!

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.570
When I was little, I really loved Miruru!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.820
I'll be going now.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.460
Really... So, you noticed, too, huh?

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.690
Yeah.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.070
Naoya is really depressed.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.480
He said the <i>Miruru</i> anime might end.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.700
What? That's a shocker.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.520
I want to help brighten 
his mood somehow, but...

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:07.060
I know!

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:10.430
Tomorrow, you and mom 
are going sightseeing in Shonan, right?

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.210
Yeah.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.370
Then let's take Naoya and all 
go on a "country bumpkins" tour.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:18.720
If we run around shouting and having fun, 
it should be a good change of pace.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.780
Right!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.860
I'm not really interested in sightseeing.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.400
Come on. Since you're here, why not?

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.950
I didn't know there was a path like this.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:33.560
Huh? This is your hometown, 
but you didn't know?

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:34.680
Yuta either?

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.740
You wouldn't think it, but it's true.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.350
The Enoshima Iwaya Caves are a cave 
system created by wave erosion.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.240
They're one of the things 
people must see in Enoshima!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.990
You're very well-versed in this.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:48.000
I've checked everything in detail!

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:56.200
The walkways in Shonan sure 
are fancy, aren't they?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.230
Not like Oarai or Oita.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.060
Right?

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.010
Could you not lump them together, please?

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.710
Oh, right!

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:07.520
They say that if you pray to the stone 
statues inside for things, it really works.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.270
Wow! How fun!

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:23.600
The ocean in Shonan really 
is different from Oarai, isn't it?

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.120
Yes, it is.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:27.890
Mount Fuji in Enoshima!

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.790
How wonderful! What a view!

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.640
It's very rare to see it 
this clearly in the summer!

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.630
This evening, we might even be 
able to see Mt. Fuji in silhouette!

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.550
Mom, we're really lucky!

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.800
Really?

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:42.520
I was just going to say all that.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.850
I think Sakura-chan might know more 
about Shonan than you.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.660
No, she doesn't!

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:54.040
Huh?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.060
What? Again?

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Misaki Diner</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Shirasu-don</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>yen</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Shonan Meal Set</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>yen</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Daily Lunch Special</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>yen</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Salt Grilled Mackerel</b>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>yen</b>

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:04.060
Welcome!

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.980
I recommend the shirasu-don.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.330
It all looks delicious!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.080
Oh! Sweet-soy-brined shirasu. How unusual.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.270
Order a shirasu-don for me.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:21.370
Hey, why is Miruru all over the place?

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.170
At this rate, it's not gonna 
help change Naoya's mood!

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:27.650
The first season of Miruru 
was set around here!

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:29.720
It's a place of pilgrimage for fans!

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.120
A place of pilgrimage... 
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:36.190
Well, I didn't know they'd have 
collaborations all over the place like this!

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.160
Okay! Let's head to Kamakura!

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.730
I'm sure Miruru won't be in Kamakura!

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.490
She's in Kamakura, too!

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.720
I haven't been here in forever.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.580
I haven't been since elementary school.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.530
This statue kind of reminds me of Dad.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.090
Oh! It does look like him!

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.640
Do you want to go inside?

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.100
Oh! Want to eat ice cream?

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.100
It's Miruru! How cute!

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:14.710
Who is this girl? I don't know her.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:17.230
It's not Periri. Who is she?

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.080
It must be Miruru's big sister!

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.610
No, it's Miruru's little sister.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:23.560
Big sister!

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.610
Little sister!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.300
That's Miruru's buddy MaiMai!

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.090
They're in the same grade 
and grew up together!

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:32.870
She's not her big sister 
or her little sister!

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:37.710
<i>Miruru First</i> came out five years ago, 
and it was set in Shonan!

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.880
And Kamakura was used 
as a location just once.

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:44.380
What you're holding is collaboration 
merchandise recreating that scene!

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:48.390
What I'm saying is, you really 
should check out <i>Miruru</i> from <i>First</i>!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.800
You can understand the story 
if you watch from the second season,

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.890
but there are so many characters 
that only appear in the first season!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.260
Naoya!

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:03.360
You're actually really...

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.280
Ow!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:09.860
Mom?

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.940
Are you all right?

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:17.660
I'm such a klutz to twist my 
ankle in a place like this.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.840
There don't seem to be any taxis coming.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.750
What a bother. I'm really so sorry.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:38.180
Hey, guys and ladies!

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:39.310
Tadao-san?

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.690
Huh? A motorcycle?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.520
Perfect timing!

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:45.440
Tadao-san! Would you let my mom ride?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.440
Yeah! Of course!

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:53.360
No one called him or anything, right?

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:56.650
So it was just coincidence? 
But that was just way too cool.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:58.960
Shonan's greatest must-see!

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.780
I really am sorry about this!

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:05.840
No problem! Now, we'll become the wind.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.840
Are you ready?

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.340
Yay!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.770
Oh, yes! Come together! Yeah!

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.690
Should we head back to the beach?

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.250
Yes, let's.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.020
Naoya, I'm sorry.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:24.050
It was wrong of me to try 
to force you to have fun.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.230
But you're wrong, too!

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.800
You can't run from Miruru!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.990
When I saw you earlier, 
that's what I thought.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.710
You really love Miruru.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:41.020
You won't be able to lock that feeling away!

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.500
What about it?

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.240
I can't really explain it, but...

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.790
At this rate, your surfing 
won't be any good.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.510
Like... no Miruru, no surfing.

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:56.140
What's that supposed to mean? I can surf.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.040
Rend the darkness!

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.040
Meteor Fan—

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:32.080
Okay!

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:36.030
Raven-Dark Blue Angel—

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.870
It's just as Hinaoka says.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.330
I'm no good.

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.340
I am powerless.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:55.670
As you are now, maybe.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.160
But there's still something 
you can do, Naoya.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.660
Win at the Forest Cup in Tsurigasaki!

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.090
With that board!

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:21.380
You told us, right? About Miruru.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:30.360
Dreams and hope... Miruru is the one 
who taught me about all of that.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:34.860
Then, this time, you can be the one 
giving dreams and hope to Miruru, right?

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.120
Through surfing!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.020
Through surfing?

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:38.870
Yeah!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.260
Even if the anime ends, you can keep 
going through surfing, right?

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:43.890
It all depends on you, Naoya!

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:49.500
If you keep surfing, and keep delivering 
amazing tricks over and over,

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.000
you'll be able to make Miruru shine, right?

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:57.490
Depending on me... Miruru can shine?

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:03.010
"We will not be defeated 
by any twists of fate!" Right?

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:08.520
We will not be defeated 
by any twists of fate!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.020
Together, we will overcome any pain!

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.160
Right? The show must go on.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:37.280
Now is the time! Revolution Change!

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:41.180
Possibilities are infinite!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:45.320
MiruMiru! MaiMai! Revolution Change!

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:53.620
Miruru...

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.360
Let's go!

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.220
Okay. Time for practice!

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.300
Yes, it is.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.430
All right!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:16.210
<i>Last time, at the competition in Oarai, 
I lost to Naoya in round 2.</i>

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.090
<i>I need to practice more and more!</i>

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:23.400
<i>I need to get better and better!</i>

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.220
<i>I've been practicing non-stop since then.</i>

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.590
<i>I won't be beat by Naoya!</i>

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:30.480
<i>And I won't lose to Fuke-san, either!</i>

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.370
All right!

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:39.860
<i>Up until now, Miruru 
has been my guardian spirit.</i>

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:43.720
<i>Now, I'll become her guardian spirit!</i>

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.880
Come, o Wings!

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.670
Innocent Exciter Miruru Forever!

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:52.120
8 fps Multiplane!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.380
Amazing!

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.360
But what did he shout just now?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:59.760
I'm not sure, but it was 
a solid air reverse.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:02.820
Masaki and Naoya are really 
giving it everything they've got.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:05.260
Guess I'd better get serious, too!

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.760
Aren't you always serious about it?

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:09.820
Did you say something?

00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:11.770
Just talking to myself.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:14.970
<i>I can't afford to stand still.</i>

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.310
<i>The Forest Cup is just a waypoint.</i>

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:20.780
<i>What I'm aiming for is far, far beyond that!</i>

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.880
<i>According to the data, 
everyone's an even match.</i>

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:28.620
<i>All that's left is to see who can catch 
that big wave of emotions!</i>

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:38.540
<i>Just like that, in aiming 
for the next competition,</i>

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:41.580
<i>out hearts were one again.</i>

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.000
Good work out there!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.850
Yeah! You're all in top condition!

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.430
There, there.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.560
That's right! It's tonight! 
The fireworks festival.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:01.070
I'd completely forgotten.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.440
I've been looking forward to it!

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:06.180
You get to see it up close, 
so it's pretty impressive.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.600
Let's go!

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:25.050
Tama-ya!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.720
Kagi-ya!

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:29.220
Miruru!

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:38.060
"The fireworks are amazing!"

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:39.650
"Just beautiful."

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:40.980
"Beautiful? You're embarrassing me."

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:44.770
<i><i>Magical Maid Miruru</i> season 6 
is going into production!</i>

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:47.520
<i>Everyone, I hope you'll support 
the continuation of our story!</i>

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.120
Wave 9
Forest Cup in Tsurigasaki
